2. Acquire a compatible .NET SDK using official Microsoft release metadata and a linux-x64 SDK archive.
   Target SDK: 10.0.201. Retrieve https://builds.dotnet.microsoft.com/dotnet/release-metadata/10.0/releases.json through Invoke-RestMethod; locate the exact SDK archive URL and SHA-512. Download using Invoke-WebRequest, validate with Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA512, extract with tar through PowerShell.MCP into /opt/mcpserver/dotnet after privileged directory creation.
   Set the build process DOTNET_ROOT and PATH to this SDK. Preserve the globally installed SDK.
   Commands after extraction: /opt/mcpserver/dotnet/dotnet --version; /opt/mcpserver/dotnet/dotnet --list-runtimes.
   Evidence: official source URL, SDK version, checksum comparison, SDK location.
   Stop: missing SDK artifact, checksum mismatch, incompatible global.json resolution.

3. Acquire plugin source checkouts in the manifest paths using the explicitly supplied repositories.
   Commands for each missing checkout: git clone <agents[].details.sourceRepository> <agents[].pluginRoot>; git -C <pluginRoot> checkout --detach <sourceCommit>; git -C <pluginRoot> rev-parse HEAD.
   Inspect existing checkout state instead of replacing it. Read each plugin's actual installation/identity contract before activation.
   The operator-specified repositories replace speculative acquisition URLs; no server tool-registry bootstrap is needed to find them.
   Evidence: each repo URL, exact commit, canonical identity, installation entry point.
   Stop: inaccessible repository, dirty/conflicting destination, identity mismatch, unsupported activation.

4. From the workspace, build the primary REPL acquisition path:
   ./build.ps1 InstallReplTool
   qbrain-ai-repl --version
   PackageId: QBrainAI.Repl. Do not also invoke plugin ensure-repl or a separate release installer.
