   Record ownership and permissions. Snapshot existing ACLs before changes.
   Grant traverse-only access to the private home directory and scoped workspace access needed by the server. Determine actual marker, TODO, context, requirements, and logging write paths from current source; keep runtime caches outside the checkout. Avoid granting the service access to unrelated private files or credentials.
   Evidence: access probes executed as mcpserver for every required path.
   Stop: access requires unreviewed broader permissions or tests fail.

3. Verify SQL authentication using the existing bootstrap credential reference without printing it or placing it in command arguments.
   Use a client that supports secret environment/input or an in-process database connection. Query server identity, database existence, and relevant login state.
   Create McpServer_Omarchy only if missing. Create a dedicated SQL login mcpserver_omarchy with a generated credential and permissions scoped to this database for the product's schema/migration needs. Do not use sa as the service account, drop an existing database, or reset an existing login password blindly.
   Store the service connection in /etc/mcpserver/mcpserver.env as Mcp__Database__SqlServer__ConnectionString. File owned by root, mode 0600; systemd reads it before switching to the service account.
   Record only secret references and non-secret server/database/login identity. Inspect TLS capability and document the chosen local SQL transport settings before creating the final connection string.
   Evidence: authenticated read-only DB identity probe; dedicated login DB access; no sysadmin role. Exception explicitly approved by operator: VIEW SERVER SECURITY STATE server metadata grant.
   Stop: invalid bootstrap credential, conflicting existing database/login, missing safe credential channel.

4. Prepare installed appsettings.yaml before starting the service. Use the complete-document YAML helper plugins/core/lib-ps/yaml-object-mutation.ps1; never edit YAML by text substitution.
   Set Mcp:Database:Provider=sqlserver, omit empty SQL connection-string keys, set Mcp:RepoRoot, and register the workspace as the enabled primary entry using the actual WorkspacePath schema.
   Remove unrelated lab workspaces/instance overrides from the installed copy. Configure service data/log paths outside the repo. Inspect current TodoStorage/provider integration and ensure any persistent store follows the selected database configuration; verify effective overlays rather than relying on labels.
   Preserve the source template. Do not hand-author trust markers.
   Copy verified publish output and the prepared YAML to /opt/mcpserver/app. Ensure the installed directory does not contain a legacy appsettings.json.
