   Stop: unsupported config schema, remaining foreign workspace/instance overrides, unintended SQLite selection.

5. Write /etc/systemd/system/mcpserver.service with:
   Type=simple
   User=mcpserver
   Group=mcpserver
   WorkingDirectory=/opt/mcpserver/app
   ExecStart=/opt/mcpserver/app/QBrainAi.Support.Mcp --urls http://localhost:7147
   EnvironmentFile=/etc/mcpserver/mcpserver.env
   StateDirectory=mcpserver
   LogsDirectory=mcpserver
   UMask=0027
   Restart=on-failure
   RestartSec=5
   WantedBy=multi-user.target
   Bound restarts with StartLimitIntervalSec/StartLimitBurst. Set service HOME to a dedicated service-owned state directory where required; do not expose operator credentials.
   Declare network/docker ordering for the existing SQL container, then verify actual SQL availability rather than treating ordering as readiness.
   Unit validation: systemd-analyze verify /etc/systemd/system/mcpserver.service.
   Start: pkexec /usr/bin/systemctl daemon-reload; pkexec /usr/bin/systemctl enable --now mcpserver.service.
   Status: systemctl show mcpserver.service -p ActiveState -p SubState -p MainPID -p User -p Group -p ExecStart; systemctl status mcpserver.service --no-pager.
   Stop: pkexec /usr/bin/systemctl stop mcpserver.service.
   Logs: pkexec /usr/bin/journalctl -u mcpserver.service -n 100 --no-pager (redact secrets before persisting).
   Evidence: validated unit, active service, expected account/executable, bounded restart behavior.
   Stop: failed unit validation or startup. After one diagnosed remediation, re-verify once; repeated failure remains blocked.

